   ],
   "abstract": "An ITIN (Individual Taxpayer Identification Number) is a 9-digit number issued by the IRS, always starting with 9, for people who need a US tax ID but cannot get a Social Security Number. It is used only for US tax purposes. You apply on Form W-7, usually alongside a US tax return."
  },
