    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Do I need an ITIN to open a US business bank account for my LLC?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "An ITIN is usually not required to open a business account for an LLC, which uses its EIN. However, some banks and fintech providers ask the owner for a personal US tax number as part of their own checks. If yours insists, an ITIN may become necessary."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does a single-member LLC owned by a UK resident file a US tax return?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A single-member LLC owned by a UK resident generally files Form 5472 with a pro-forma Form 1120 each year, using its EIN. Whether the owner must also file a personal Form 1040-NR depends on the type and source of the income."
