      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, a Certifying Acceptance Agent can verify your passport for an ITIN renewal so it stays with you. Where a video interview suits your application, you courier it to us and we return it by secure tracked post. Around Bedford and Milton Keynes we can visit you at home instead. The CAA then certifies the documents to the IRS."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "What happens if I file a US return with an expired ITIN?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A return filed with an expired ITIN may still be processed, sometimes under a temporary number, but refunds and credits are held until the ITIN is properly renewed. It's usually smoother to send a renewal Form W-7 with the return, so everything is handled together and nothing waits longer than it needs to."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How long does ITIN renewal take in 2026?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "ITIN renewal takes about 7 weeks according to the IRS, or 9 to 11 weeks in peak season (15 January to 30 April) or from abroad. In our experience, April to July can take 12 to 13 weeks, September about 7, and from October often 4 to 6. Nobody can promise a date."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "What is a temporary ITIN?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A \"temporary ITIN\" is the informal name for a temporary number the IRS may use to process a return filed with an expired ITIN. Your refund and any credits are not released until the ITIN is properly renewed. Renewal usually keeps your original ITIN number, so you do not need a brand-new one."
